WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.527
- What I do know about Hawaii.

00:00:01.527 --> 00:00:02.886
That there was a queen.

00:00:02.886 --> 00:00:06.386
You know, that's as far as it goes for me!

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.627
- I grew up in Hawaii.

00:00:11.627 --> 00:00:13.361
I went to an all-Hawaiian school.

00:00:13.361 --> 00:00:14.331
- I'm originally from Hawaii.

00:00:14.331 --> 00:00:16.746
I went to a school that
only allowed Hawaiians.

00:00:16.746 --> 00:00:18.346
- I grew up in Honolulu.

00:00:18.346 --> 00:00:20.876
- I don't claim to know
anything about Hawaiian history.

00:00:20.876 --> 00:00:21.772
- I don't remember learning

00:00:21.772 --> 00:00:24.182
any Hawaiian history back in school.

00:00:24.182 --> 00:00:25.373
Really, I don't.

00:00:25.373 --> 00:00:26.206
Except Pearl Harbor.

00:00:26.206 --> 00:00:27.764
- Being that I don't know anything,

00:00:27.764 --> 00:00:29.796
I'm pretty sure I'm not gonna do the best.

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:30.629
- I'm kind of excited to see

00:00:30.629 --> 00:00:32.396
how much I actually remember.

00:00:32.396 --> 00:00:33.796
- Let's go take this test!

00:00:33.796 --> 00:00:35.013
- [Lawrence] Who were the first people

00:00:35.013 --> 00:00:36.381
to arrive in Hawaii?

00:00:36.381 --> 00:00:38.579
- [Johanna] A, Polynesians, B, Tahitians,

00:00:38.579 --> 00:00:40.466
C, Americans?

00:00:40.466 --> 00:00:42.939
- I know someone from Fifth
Harmony that's Polynesian.

00:00:42.939 --> 00:00:43.890
- What do you think?

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.184
- You asking me for what the answer is?

00:00:45.184 --> 00:00:46.017
- Do you think you know it?

00:00:46.017 --> 00:00:46.855
- Yeah, no, I definitely know.

00:00:46.855 --> 00:00:47.785
- I think Polynesian?

00:00:47.785 --> 00:00:48.618
- I guessed Polynesian.

00:00:48.618 --> 00:00:49.936
- I said A, Polynesians.

00:00:49.936 --> 00:00:51.103
- Polynesians?

00:00:52.212 --> 00:00:53.781
- [Announcer] Polynesians is correct!

00:00:53.781 --> 00:00:54.614
- Yay!

00:00:54.614 --> 00:00:55.447
- Nice!

00:00:55.447 --> 00:00:56.280
- [Announcer] It's Polynesians.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.571
- Cool.

00:00:57.571 --> 00:00:58.780
- [Shelden] Who was the
last king of Hawaii?

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:00.312
- A, David Kalakaua,

00:01:00.312 --> 00:01:02.240
B, Kamehameha the Great,

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:06.407
C, Caesar Kaluaiku Kamaka'ehukai
Kahana Keola Kapa'akea,

00:01:09.626 --> 00:01:11.278
and D, Steve.

00:01:11.278 --> 00:01:13.614
- I mean, there's only
one that sounds right.

00:01:13.614 --> 00:01:15.582
- I'm saying David Kalakaua.

00:01:15.582 --> 00:01:17.182
- Nice, yeah, that's what I put down.

00:01:17.182 --> 00:01:18.772
- A, David Kalakaua.

00:01:18.772 --> 00:01:19.724
(bell ringing)

00:01:19.724 --> 00:01:21.284
- Wow!

00:01:21.284 --> 00:01:22.460
- Okay!

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:23.420
- Yay!

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:24.548
- [Kane] Hawaii's last king

00:01:24.548 --> 00:01:27.065
was forced to sign away
the executive powers

00:01:27.065 --> 00:01:27.898
of the monarchy.

00:01:27.898 --> 00:01:30.100
Who took over power immediately after him?

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.508
- [Johanna] A, the people of Hawaii,

00:01:31.508 --> 00:01:34.308
B, US Businessmen, C, the people of Kona,

00:01:34.308 --> 00:01:35.988
D, The US Government.

00:01:35.988 --> 00:01:37.378
- Oh God.

00:01:37.378 --> 00:01:38.643
- I think it's the US Government.

00:01:38.643 --> 00:01:39.476
- Who you going for?

00:01:39.476 --> 00:01:40.309
- US Government.

00:01:40.309 --> 00:01:41.298
- Yeah, that's what I put down.

00:01:41.298 --> 00:01:43.370
- I put US Businessmen.

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:44.514
- US Businessmen?

00:01:44.514 --> 00:01:46.299
- [Announcer] The answer
is US Businessmen.

00:01:46.299 --> 00:01:47.553
- I mean it doesn't surprise me,

00:01:47.553 --> 00:01:49.487
I feel like businessmen
have as much or more power

00:01:49.487 --> 00:01:51.095
than the government in our country.

00:01:51.095 --> 00:01:54.074
- They held the economy,
so, money talks, I guess.

00:01:54.074 --> 00:01:55.101
- It makes me feel really sad.

00:01:55.101 --> 00:01:56.253
I didn't even know that.

00:01:56.253 --> 00:01:58.581
- [Shelden] In the 1890's,
Hawaii's last ruler,

00:01:58.581 --> 00:02:00.309
Queen Lili'uokalani was

00:02:00.309 --> 00:02:03.093
- [Lawrence] A, imprisoned,
B, forced to abdicate,

00:02:03.093 --> 00:02:05.109
C, stripped of her power illegally,

00:02:05.109 --> 00:02:06.437
D, all of the above.

00:02:06.437 --> 00:02:08.170
- Forced to abdicate?

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:09.580
I'm just completely
guessing at this point.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:10.996
- I'm going to say all
of the above, I think.

00:02:10.996 --> 00:02:12.188
- I'm going to say all of the above.

00:02:12.188 --> 00:02:13.132
- D.

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:14.681
- [Announcer] The answer
is all of the above.

00:02:14.681 --> 00:02:15.721
- You guess all of the above?

00:02:15.721 --> 00:02:18.913
- Yep. She was imprisoned
in her own palace.

00:02:18.913 --> 00:02:21.055
- Like someone going into your
house and just being like,

00:02:21.055 --> 00:02:22.248
you can't do anything here.

00:02:22.248 --> 00:02:23.988
Go in your room and stay there.

00:02:23.988 --> 00:02:24.834
- [Kane] After the overthrow

00:02:24.834 --> 00:02:27.331
of the Hawaiian kingdom in 1893,

00:02:27.331 --> 00:02:28.828
which of these were banned?

00:02:28.828 --> 00:02:30.468
- [Alison] A, Speaking Hawaiian in school,

00:02:30.468 --> 00:02:32.484
B, Consumption of Hawaiian dishes,

00:02:32.484 --> 00:02:34.700
C, Planting of Hawaiian flowers,

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.012
D, All of the above.

00:02:36.012 --> 00:02:37.883
- I mean, it's A.

00:02:37.883 --> 00:02:39.016
- I definitely think it's A.

00:02:39.016 --> 00:02:41.433
- I put A, speaking Hawaiian in school.

00:02:41.433 --> 00:02:42.792
- Same.

00:02:42.792 --> 00:02:43.856
- [Announcer] That's correct.

00:02:43.856 --> 00:02:45.112
- My grandma, she didn't really get

00:02:45.112 --> 00:02:45.945
to speak Hawaiian.

00:02:45.945 --> 00:02:47.080
She didn't really know

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:49.616
about some of the Hawaiian
traditions and everything.

00:02:49.616 --> 00:02:52.296
- In a culture where
history and information

00:02:52.296 --> 00:02:54.640
is passed down through word of mouth,

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:58.587
by erasing the language,
you erase the memory.

00:02:58.587 --> 00:02:59.441
- [Leimana] Which of these

00:02:59.441 --> 00:03:00.274
is believed to be a reason

00:03:00.274 --> 00:03:02.003
why hula dancing was banned?

00:03:02.003 --> 00:03:03.803
- [Lawrence] A, Hula made Hawaiians

00:03:03.803 --> 00:03:05.206
lazy and unwilling to work,

00:03:05.206 --> 00:03:07.404
B, Hula threatened the
ability to convert people

00:03:07.404 --> 00:03:09.883
to Christianity and was therefore evil,

00:03:09.883 --> 00:03:14.207
C, it was a heathen practice
for physical pleasure,

00:03:14.207 --> 00:03:15.327
D, all of the above.

00:03:15.327 --> 00:03:16.219
- This is ridiculous,

00:03:16.219 --> 00:03:17.900
I can't believe it was even banned.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.215
- I feel like it's all of the above.

00:03:20.215 --> 00:03:21.743
- I think it's Hula threatened the ability

00:03:21.743 --> 00:03:23.271
to convert people to Christianity.

00:03:23.271 --> 00:03:24.615
- I put the same one.

00:03:24.615 --> 00:03:25.543
- [Announcer] It was all of the above.

00:03:25.543 --> 00:03:26.519
- Damn it!

00:03:26.519 --> 00:03:28.903
- I grew up dancing
hula, dancing Tahitian,

00:03:28.903 --> 00:03:31.880
I can't imagine not having it in my life.

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:33.111
- [Shelden] After the
attack on Pearl Harbor,

00:03:33.111 --> 00:03:34.825
how did the US use the Hawaiian Islands

00:03:34.825 --> 00:03:36.448
to prepare for the war?

00:03:36.448 --> 00:03:37.616
- [Alison] A, hiding missiles

00:03:37.616 --> 00:03:38.962
within Hawaiian water supplies,

00:03:38.962 --> 00:03:41.416
B, placing a specific tax on Hawaiians

00:03:41.416 --> 00:03:42.249
to pay for weapons,

00:03:42.249 --> 00:03:45.403
C, using one of the
islands as a bombing range,

00:03:45.403 --> 00:03:48.404
D, putting underaged
Hawaiians into the army.

00:03:48.404 --> 00:03:49.609
- This one's hard.

00:03:49.609 --> 00:03:51.026
- No all of the above for this one,

00:03:51.026 --> 00:03:53.122
which I feel like, wouldn't be crazy.

00:03:53.122 --> 00:03:54.626
- I'm guessing it's either water supply,

00:03:54.626 --> 00:03:56.826
or like, using an island
as a bombing range.

00:03:56.826 --> 00:03:59.298
- I put B, C, and D.

00:03:59.298 --> 00:04:01.342
- C, using an island as a bombing range?

00:04:01.342 --> 00:04:02.290
- [Announcer] Yep, that's correct.

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:04.794
- You can't really get to the island

00:04:04.794 --> 00:04:07.595
unless you go through
a certain organization,

00:04:07.595 --> 00:04:09.090
because otherwise you might trigger

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:11.386
a bomb that hasn't exploded yet.

00:04:11.386 --> 00:04:13.275
- This test is a hard test.

00:04:13.275 --> 00:04:15.139
It's also exciting to get it right,

00:04:15.139 --> 00:04:16.547
but then it's like, oh shit,

00:04:16.547 --> 00:04:17.813
this is really sad.

00:04:17.813 --> 00:04:19.141
- [Johanna] When did Hawaii officially

00:04:19.141 --> 00:04:21.365
receive an apology from
the US government for its

00:04:21.365 --> 00:04:23.063
role in starting the coup?

00:04:23.063 --> 00:04:24.702
- [Leimana] A, 50 years after the coup,

00:04:24.702 --> 00:04:26.839
B, immediately after their statehood,

00:04:26.839 --> 00:04:29.134
C, after US military bases left,

00:04:29.134 --> 00:04:30.814
D, 100 years after the coup.

00:04:30.814 --> 00:04:32.666
- I don't know because I don't remember

00:04:32.666 --> 00:04:34.247
there being an apology.

00:04:34.247 --> 00:04:35.358
- Maybe 100 years.

00:04:35.358 --> 00:04:36.255
I think it's D.

00:04:36.255 --> 00:04:37.334
- Yeah, I think it's D as well.

00:04:37.334 --> 00:04:38.167
- [Announcer] That's correct.

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:39.254
- 100 years!

00:04:39.254 --> 00:04:42.095
- 1993, Bill Clinton
signed a formal apology

00:04:42.095 --> 00:04:43.583
to our kingdom.

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:45.383
- They feel like it's okay to
just give them that credit,

00:04:45.383 --> 00:04:46.270
then they can move on,

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:49.019
but give people their stuff back.

00:04:49.019 --> 00:04:50.734
- [Leimana] On July 12, 1898,

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:52.270
the US formally annexed Hawaii.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:53.870
However, international law dictates

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:55.694
that annexation treaties must by signed

00:04:55.694 --> 00:04:56.918
by both countries involved.

00:04:56.918 --> 00:04:58.518
This did not occur in Hawaii.

00:04:58.518 --> 00:05:02.018
Given this information, is Hawaii a state?

00:05:03.646 --> 00:05:07.477
- To be technical, Hawaii
is a illegal occupation.

00:05:07.477 --> 00:05:08.714
- These are, like, you know,

00:05:08.714 --> 00:05:10.721
laws that Hawaii never agreed to

00:05:10.721 --> 00:05:13.193
in the first place as
far as being a state.

00:05:13.193 --> 00:05:15.321
- I don't think it is a state,

00:05:15.321 --> 00:05:17.419
just because of international law

00:05:17.419 --> 00:05:19.390
that is still kind of
disputed to this day.

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:21.680
- You know, there are of
course, varying attitudes,

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:23.209
but, I mean, yeah, the fact of the matter

00:05:23.209 --> 00:05:26.392
is the US took Hawaii
and called it a state.

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:28.017
It was a cool test.

00:05:28.017 --> 00:05:29.504
I like that it highlights these issues,

00:05:29.504 --> 00:05:31.921
but I feel like this was
an American history test

00:05:31.921 --> 00:05:33.782
on the subject of Hawaii,

00:05:33.782 --> 00:05:36.453
rather than a Hawaiian history test.

00:05:36.453 --> 00:05:37.726
- I learned so much today,

00:05:37.726 --> 00:05:40.699
I think how we view Hawaii in America

00:05:40.699 --> 00:05:42.753
is just like a vacation paradise.

00:05:42.753 --> 00:05:43.769
If we learned this in school,

00:05:43.769 --> 00:05:45.213
we would be in a different frame of mind.

00:05:45.213 --> 00:05:46.816
- Everyone should understand

00:05:46.816 --> 00:05:47.912
what land they're visiting,

00:05:47.912 --> 00:05:50.113
and where they're building things on.

00:05:50.113 --> 00:05:51.233
- I knew a lot of the facts,

00:05:51.233 --> 00:05:52.842
I'm going to a Hawaiian school,

00:05:52.842 --> 00:05:54.609
but I didn't really know the full context.

00:05:54.609 --> 00:05:55.832
This was really enlightening.

00:05:55.832 --> 00:05:57.248
- It was really nice to
learn all this stuff,

00:05:57.248 --> 00:05:58.953
and I definitely want to learn more

00:05:58.953 --> 00:06:00.769
about Hawaii before the US,

00:06:00.769 --> 00:06:04.936
and I wish that I'd sought
out this information earlier.

